ONEDRAFT
CAD-AI — Aria Powered
Testing, Quality Assurance & Verification System
Version 1.0
Status: Implementation Specification
System: OneDraft CAD-AI Platform
Subsystem: Testing, Quality Assurance & Verification
Primary Objective: Establish the automated and deterministic mechanisms by which OneDraft verifies the correctness, integrity, reproducibility, safety, and operational reliability of its software, computational project model, geometry, compliance analysis, documentation, runtime services, and generated deliverables.

1. TESTING SYSTEM PRINCIPLE
Testing is a first-class subsystem of OneDraft.
OneDraft shall not treat testing as a final development activity performed after implementation.
Testing shall exist continuously across:
source code
domain services
database
API
geometry
parametric relationships
compliance
validation
documentation
AI commands
runtime orchestration
workers
artifacts
security
integrations
user workflows
and:
final project acceptance
The testing system therefore becomes an independent verification layer over the OneDraft computational system.
The objective is not merely to determine whether software executes.
The objective is to determine whether the system produces the correct project state from defined inputs while preserving constraints, provenance, version integrity, regulatory evidence, and reproducibility.

2. QUALITY ASSURANCE PRINCIPLE
OneDraft shall distinguish between:
Testing
determining whether a defined behavior produces the expected result.
Verification
determining whether the implementation satisfies its technical specification.
Validation
determining whether the resulting project state satisfies defined requirements, constraints, rules, and acceptance criteria.
Quality assurance
establishing the processes and controls that make those outcomes repeatable.
The four concepts shall remain related but distinct.

