OneDraft shall treat automated verification as part of the computational architecture rather than as an external development convenience.
The system must continuously answer:
Did the software execute correctly?

Did the domain model remain valid?

Did the geometry remain valid?

Were constraints preserved?

Was the applicable regulatory state preserved?

Was validation performed?

Were the drawings generated from the correct revision?

Was the document package generated from the correct model?

Was the artifact preserved?

Can the result be reconstructed?

Can the result be independently verified?
The answer to each question must be represented through executable tests, structured records, or deterministic verification mechanisms.
Testing therefore becomes part of the OneDraft system of evidence.

